{'symbol': 'PPL', 'date': '2022-12-15 14:41:00', 'title': "PPL CORPORATION'S KENTUCKY UTILITIES FILE PLAN TO REPLACE 1,500 MEGAWATTS OF AGING GENERATION BY 2028", 'text': "LG&E AND KU SEEK TO ADD NATURAL GAS, SOLAR AND ENERGY STORAGE, ALONG WITH MORE THAN A DOZEN NEW ENERGY EFFICIENCY PROGRAMS ALLENTOWN, PA. , DEC. 15, 2022 \xa0(DEC. 15, 2022) – PPL CORPORATION (NYSE: PPL) SUBSIDIARIES LOUISVILLE GAS AND ELECTRIC COMPANY AND KENTUCKY UTILITIES COMPANY ANNOUNCED TODAY THEIR PLAN TO REPLACE 1,500 MEGAWATTS OF AGING COAL-FIRED GENERATION, OR NEARLY ONE-THIRD OF KENTUCKY'S COAL FLEET, THAT IS EXPECTED TO BE RETIRED BY 2028."}